From a85ab74bf415502eaa19ef4054a9281564f91c7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:59:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer: give decorated freeform tasks their own window
 geometry

Collect task layer bounds, use task-local subsurface positions and fit the
native parent to the task instead of framing the whole Android display.
Keep each task at the output scale; a per-app configure must not reshape
the shared display or affect other apps.

Remember native client dimensions separately from Android buffer bounds,
so arriving frames cannot undo a host resize. Fit old buffers uniformly
while Android relays out the task, and apply the inverse viewport mapping
to pointer, touch and tablet input. Android client-side shadow insets must
be disabled with render_shadows_in_compositor=1 when using SSD.

Coalesce host configures for 100 ms on a per-window worker, then resize only
that task through app_process and ActivityTaskManager.resizeTask.
Binder shellCommand rejects the composer's system UID, so the optional SSD
Java helper calls the task API directly instead. This also handles maximize and
tiling, without requiring a final non-resizing configure or feeding our own
geometry updates back into another task resize. Reap commands off-thread;
window destruction never waits for WindowManager.

Original work for waydroid-nvidia; modifies Apache-2.0 hwcomposer sources.
